                    {
                        "translation_id": "e34d8b5c-440b-4b7e-a801-6bbc5a036b55",
                        "source_entry_id": "5e1a1af0-90db-3593-ad42-b384b605b414",
                        "source_sense_id": "bd857ad9-f5a5-37fc-8119-6c9e4d506692",
                        "target_lang_word": "liverwort",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "liverwort",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a441be4e-3940-33fe-bf8e-73955cfbb2fd",
                                        "entry_id": "a0be2564-27bf-365c-81a8-9a4c6545dee7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of bryophyte with a leafy stem or leafless thallus characterized by a dominant gametophyte stage and a lack of stomata on the sporophyte stage of the life cycle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e00ee116-e531-465a-998e-b4494b946a09",
                                                "sense_id": "a441be4e-3940-33fe-bf8e-73955cfbb2fd",
                                                "text": "The liverworts are either thallose, without any differentiation into stem and leaves, or leafy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "037e41da-a681-43d3-8f4f-04589633d89e",
                                                "sense_id": "a441be4e-3940-33fe-bf8e-73955cfbb2fd",
                                                "text": "Since the thallus of some liverworts resembled a liver, such plants were considered useful in making a concoction that would aid in curing liver ailments. Hence the name \"liver-plant,\" or liverwort. Unfortunately, there is no evidence that liverworts possess curative properties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "402af4be-dc7e-4939-a261-a4adbd4e83d1",
                                                "sense_id": "a441be4e-3940-33fe-bf8e-73955cfbb2fd",
                                                "text": "2000 — Barbara Crandall-Stotler & Raymond E. Stotler, \"Morphology and classification of the Marchantiophyta\". pages 21-70 in A. Jonathan Shaw & Bernard Goffinet (Eds.), Bryophyte Biology, page 21.\nLike other bryophytes, liverworts are small, herbaceous plants of terrestrial ecosystems."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35ffff07-b34a-3b1f-b7b1-a4c2787c1a4f",
